# Job Application Screener — Cursor Rules

## Project
CPVC Build Night project. Node.js/Express backend + vanilla HTML/CSS/JS frontend.
Screens job applicants using Groq's Llama 3.3 70B model.

## Stack
- Runtime: Node.js
- Framework: Express (server.js)
- AI: Groq SDK (groq-sdk package), model: llama-3.3-70b-versatile
- Frontend: Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS in public/index.html — no frameworks, no build step
- Config: dotenv, GROQ_API_KEY in .env (never commit .env)

## File structure
- server.js        — Express server + /screen POST endpoint + Groq API call
- public/index.html — entire frontend (input form + results rendering in one file)
- .env             — GROQ_API_KEY=... (local only, gitignored)
- .env.example     — template, safe to commit

## Running locally
npm install && npm start
Open http://localhost:3000

## Key conventions
- The /screen endpoint expects JSON body: { jobDescription, resume }
- Groq response_format is json_object — always parse completion.choices[0].message.content
- Frontend is a single page — results render in-place via JS, no page reload
- Do not add a frontend framework or build tool unless explicitly asked
- Do not commit .env or any API keys

## Groq response shape
{
  decision: "ADVANCE" | "REJECT",
  confidence: "High" | "Medium" | "Low",
  summary: string,
  scores: { skills_match, experience_level, education_fit, overall_fit }, // 0-100
  strengths: string[],
  gaps: string[],
  decision_reason: string
}
